      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A case of idiopathic cryoagglutininaemia, with cryoglobulinaemia and lymphoplasmacytoid infiltration of the bone marrow is reported. The case is not held to be an independent clinical entity but an aspect of immunoproliferative disease, similar to Waldenstrom's disease. An association of steroids in high doses and cyclophosphamide led to a definite improvement in the clinical and haematological picture and this has continued for the past 4 years with little or no treatment."},
